#import "../../../proofs.typ": speech, footnote

== 23. Of Lawful Oaths And Vows

#speech[#smallcaps[Paragraph 1]: A lawful oath is a part of religious worship, wherein the person swearing in truth, righteousness, and judgment, solemnly calls God to witness what he swears,#footnote[Exodus 20:7; Deuteronomy 10:20; Jeremiah 4:2] and to judge him according to the truth or falseness thereof.#footnote[2 Chronicles 6:22–23]]

#speech[#smallcaps[Paragraph 2]: The name of God only is that by which men ought to swear; and therein it is to be used, with all holy fear and reverence; therefore to swear vainly or rashly by that glorious and dreadful name, or to swear at all by any other thing, is sinful, and to be abhorred;#footnote[Matthew 5:34, 37; James 5:12] yet as in matter of weight and moment, for confirmation of truth, and ending all strife, an oath is warranted by the Word of God;#footnote[Hebrews 6:16; 2 Corinthians 1:23] so a lawful oath being imposed by lawful authority in such matters, ought to be taken.#footnote[Nehemiah 13:25]]

#speech[#smallcaps[Paragraph 3]: Whosoever taketh an oath warranted by the Word of God, ought duly to consider the weightiness of so solemn an act, and therein to avouch nothing but what he knoweth to be truth; for that by rash, false, and vain oaths, the Lord is provoked, and for them this land mourns.#footnote[Leviticus 19:12; Jeremiah 23:10]]

#speech[#smallcaps[Paragraph 4]: An oath is to be taken in the plain and common sense of the words, without equivocation or mental reservation.#footnote[Psalm 24:4]]

#speech[#smallcaps[Paragraph 5]: A vow, which is not to be made to any creature, but to God alone, is to be made and performed with all religious care and faithfulness;#footnote[Psalm 76:11; Genesis 28:20–22] but popish monastical vows of perpetual single life,#footnote[1 Corinthians 7:2, 9] professed poverty,#footnote[Ephesians 4:28] and regular obedience, are so far from being degrees of higher perfection, that they are superstitious and sinful snares, in which no Christian may entangle himself.#footnote[Matthew 19:1]]
